[slope] This is the rear end of the open display-component channel at S47.24. It bounds the hardware insertion clearance. In the tip's +40 degree print pose, the dispense face is on the bed and this rear wall faces down. The retained faucet-display-petgf native slice carries it with bed-rooted tree-1, interface-1 at print Z46.28 through Z46.76, after 46.08 mm of build-up. The opening admits support removal before loading the display; physical removal and contact finish remain print observations.
